Claim: \lambda_1^X(D) = r(1 - \mu_1) < \frac{r}{|D|} \int_D \int_{D^c} j(y-x) \, dy \, dx \text{ because the principal eigenfunction is not constant in } L^2(D). Direct numerical evaluation on } D=(-1, 1) \text{ with standard Gaussian jump density yields } \mu_1 \approx 1.77857 > \frac{1}{|D|} \int_D \int_D j(y-x) dx dy \approx 1.77387, \text{ so the formula } (2.1) \text{ is false.} 
